1
00:00:25,247 --> 00:00:26,386
(On a particularly sweltering day in August)

2
00:00:26,387 --> 00:00:28,747
We're in Dongjak-gu.

3
00:00:29,417 --> 00:00:31,487
They're giving us tasty refreshments today.

4
00:00:33,487 --> 00:00:35,557
- Did you have breakfast?
- I did.

5
00:00:35,927 --> 00:00:36,957
What did you have?

6
00:00:37,057 --> 00:00:39,896
Well, I had some rice with eggs...

7
00:00:39,897 --> 00:00:41,167
and japchae.

8
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:42,866
- So...
- You have a nice breakfast.

9
00:00:42,867 --> 00:00:44,587
- You had japchae for breakfast?
- My gosh.

10
00:00:44,997 --> 00:00:46,236
- My breakfast is always nice.
- Really?

11
00:00:46,237 --> 00:00:47,466
(He had quite the breakfast.)

12
00:00:47,467 --> 00:00:48,467
I enjoyed my breakfast.

13
00:00:48,468 --> 00:00:50,476
People rarely get to have japchae for breakfast.

14
00:00:50,477 --> 00:00:52,076
We're filming the show...

15
00:00:52,077 --> 00:00:53,517
- in the middle of the day.
- I see.

16
00:00:55,077 --> 00:00:56,316
- The fact that they don't know...
- I'm nervous.

17
00:00:56,317 --> 00:00:57,517
We're coming...

18
00:00:58,217 --> 00:00:59,747
is kind of crazy.

19
00:01:00,217 --> 00:01:02,487
I mean, they need to be prepared in some way.

20
00:01:03,017 --> 00:01:04,586
But Jae Seok seems to manage without any preparation.

21
00:01:04,587 --> 00:01:06,757
Really? That's fascinating.

22
00:01:07,557 --> 00:01:09,457
- I think it's this way.
- This way.

23
00:01:09,757 --> 00:01:11,457
I see. What a unique location for a cafe.

24
00:01:12,727 --> 00:01:14,227
Wait. This is quite sudden.

25
00:01:14,497 --> 00:01:15,967
- Is that Hae In?
- Wait. Sung Tae!

26
00:01:16,897 --> 00:01:17,936
- Who's that?
- Hae In.

27
00:01:17,937 --> 00:01:18,967
- What?
- Hello.

28
00:01:20,267 --> 00:01:22,637
(With his youthful looks, )

29
00:01:22,837 --> 00:01:25,183
(this young guy made the hearts of many older women flutter.)

30
00:01:25,207 --> 00:01:26,976
(With one gesture...)

31
00:01:26,977 --> 00:01:28,747
(and one line, )

32
00:01:28,847 --> 00:01:30,777
(the viewers were instantly won over.)

33
00:01:31,117 --> 00:01:34,117
(A top-tier actor with incredible genre versatility)

34
00:01:36,257 --> 00:01:38,587
(Actor Jung Hae In)

35
00:01:39,287 --> 00:01:42,167
(The biggest villain in "Squid Game" that kept the entire world on edge)

36
00:01:42,287 --> 00:01:44,457
(He can pull off playing a gangster role...)

37
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:46,927
(and a detective role.)

38
00:01:47,227 --> 00:01:49,747
(Actor Heo Sung Tae can even pull off playing a romantic role.)

39
00:01:49,967 --> 00:01:52,737
(The two lead actors from "Our Sticky Love")

40
00:01:53,707 --> 00:01:55,707
- Hello.
- Hello.

41
00:01:56,537 --> 00:01:58,136
(Happy to see him)

42
00:01:58,137 --> 00:01:59,206
- Sung Tae.
- My gosh.

43
00:01:59,207 --> 00:02:01,346
- Mr. Lawyer.
- My goodness.

44
00:02:01,347 --> 00:02:02,947
- What's going on?
- Sung Tae.

45
00:02:03,417 --> 00:02:05,117
- Let's sit down.
- Okay.

46
00:02:06,387 --> 00:02:07,387
Hae In.

47
00:02:07,388 --> 00:02:09,086
- It's been a while, Hae In.
- Gosh.

48
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:11,016
We met briefly when we were both filming.

49
00:02:11,017 --> 00:02:12,556
- Remember?
- Yes. We did.

50
00:02:12,557 --> 00:02:13,926
- I was filming an SBS drama.
- Yes.

51
00:02:13,927 --> 00:02:16,456
- He was filming his new drama then.
- Oh, right.

52
00:02:16,457 --> 00:02:18,326
- He was filming in the next studio.
- It was at the same company.

53
00:02:18,327 --> 00:02:19,726
- I went to say hello to him.
- Oh, right.

54
00:02:19,727 --> 00:02:21,526
He rushed over and said hello.

55
00:02:21,527 --> 00:02:24,667
- Gosh, he's one polite guy.
- Yes. My gosh.

56
00:02:24,967 --> 00:02:26,736
I didn't know you guys were joining us today.

57
00:02:26,737 --> 00:02:28,866
I wanted to ask him to take on my case.

58
00:02:28,867 --> 00:02:30,106
- He played a ghost in the drama.
- Oh, right.

59
00:02:30,107 --> 00:02:31,376
- You were both in the drama.
- In "Phantom Lawyer."

60
00:02:31,377 --> 00:02:33,647
- "Phantom Lawyer."
- He had a really tough role.

61
00:02:34,077 --> 00:02:36,016
- Why?
- He was in Episodes 1 and 2.

62
00:02:36,017 --> 00:02:37,776
- I see.
- He played a ghost,

63
00:02:37,777 --> 00:02:39,516
so he had to film the same scenes twice...

64
00:02:39,517 --> 00:02:40,993
because he had to be seen and then disappear.

65
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:42,537
He was constantly strapped into wires.

66
00:02:43,187 --> 00:02:45,417
I had the most fun experience while filming the drama.

67
00:02:45,557 --> 00:02:47,087
I had to be up in the air.

68
00:02:47,487 --> 00:02:50,657
I didn't have any special equipment. I just delivered my lines.

69
00:02:50,797 --> 00:02:52,126
(He had to make it look like he was floating.)

70
00:02:52,127 --> 00:02:54,026
- You had to do that? I get it.
- Yes, I had to do it.

71
00:02:54,027 --> 00:02:56,096
- His character was floating.
- You were floating in the air.

72
00:02:56,097 --> 00:02:57,713
- That was a new kind of experience.
- That's...

73
00:02:57,737 --> 00:02:59,436
(He's pretending that he's floating.)

74
00:02:59,437 --> 00:03:00,937
(Floating)

75
00:03:01,207 --> 00:03:02,977
One day, they gave him a gym ball.

76
00:03:04,577 --> 00:03:06,446
He got the gym ball and sat on it.

77
00:03:06,447 --> 00:03:07,906
- Right. I know.
- So...

78
00:03:07,907 --> 00:03:09,316
he had to pretend he was floating.

79
00:03:09,317 --> 00:03:10,377
That was a new experience.

80
00:03:12,347 --> 00:03:14,646
- I knew that Hae In's new drama...
- Yes.

81
00:03:14,647 --> 00:03:16,987
- was going to air soon.
- Right.

82
00:03:17,287 --> 00:03:19,826
- The title is "Our Sticky Love."
- Yes.

83
00:03:19,827 --> 00:03:21,356
- So...
- Is it called sticky...

84
00:03:21,357 --> 00:03:22,826
because you can't be separated?

85
00:03:22,827 --> 00:03:24,027
- My gosh.
- I see.

86
00:03:24,157 --> 00:03:25,357
- Of course.
- I knew it.

87
00:03:25,427 --> 00:03:26,643
- That's the meaning behind it?
- Yes.

88
00:03:26,667 --> 00:03:27,796
- Yes.
- It's sweet and sticky like taffy.

89
00:03:27,797 --> 00:03:29,517
- It's sweet too.
- It's sticky like taffy.

90
00:03:29,597 --> 00:03:30,866
I watched the trailer.

91
00:03:30,867 --> 00:03:32,496
She has amnesia in the drama.

92
00:03:32,497 --> 00:03:33,537
Right.

93
00:03:33,937 --> 00:03:35,567
She has amnesia.

94
00:03:35,867 --> 00:03:38,676
And I'm insisting that I'm her boyfriend.

95
00:03:38,677 --> 00:03:41,807
In a way, I'm tricking her into falling in love with me.

96
00:03:42,307 --> 00:03:44,447
(A prosecutor loses her memory while chasing a case.)

97
00:03:44,547 --> 00:03:45,877
(Jang Tae Ha, the boyfriend)

98
00:03:46,787 --> 00:03:50,257
(Tangled between the truth and secrets)

99
00:03:50,717 --> 00:03:52,917
(A sweet and suspenseful romance with an amnesia twist)

100
00:03:53,087 --> 00:03:54,656
(It's available on the streaming website.)

101
00:03:54,657 --> 00:03:56,226
But that sounds like a nice deal.

102
00:03:56,227 --> 00:03:57,797
- She doesn't have any memory.
- Okay.

103
00:03:58,097 --> 00:03:59,667
One day, she just wakes up.

104
00:03:59,927 --> 00:04:01,766
Hae In comes and tells her he's her boyfriend.

105
00:04:01,767 --> 00:04:02,897
- Right.
- Yes.

106
00:04:03,797 --> 00:04:05,066
So you're the villain...

107
00:04:05,067 --> 00:04:06,207
in their love story, right?

108
00:04:06,607 --> 00:04:08,507
- You're the villain.
- Yes.

109
00:04:08,767 --> 00:04:11,036
I make a sticky mess.

110
00:04:11,037 --> 00:04:12,206
- Watch your pronunciation.
- I see.

111
00:04:12,207 --> 00:04:14,106
- He's a supervillain.
- A villain?

112
00:04:14,107 --> 00:04:15,646
- Really?
- It's been a while.

113
00:04:15,647 --> 00:04:17,546
It's been three years since I last played...

114
00:04:17,547 --> 00:04:18,877
- Really?
- a villain.

115
00:04:19,017 --> 00:04:20,146
I've been mostly playing detectives.

116
00:04:20,147 --> 00:04:21,523
It felt just like riding a bicycle, right?

117
00:04:21,547 --> 00:04:23,427
- But the thing is...
- It was easy, wasn't it?

118
00:04:23,857 --> 00:04:25,956
When we started filming and running lines...

119
00:04:25,957 --> 00:04:27,756
in the beginning, it didn't hit me.

120
00:04:27,757 --> 00:04:30,457
Then we did a scene where blood splattered on my face.

121
00:04:30,857 --> 00:04:32,527
Once blood splashed on my face,

122
00:04:32,967 --> 00:04:34,027
I thought, "This is it."

123
00:04:35,097 --> 00:04:36,536
So this is what I said to the director.

124
00:04:36,537 --> 00:04:37,867
"I'm getting the hang of it now."

125
00:04:38,097 --> 00:04:40,383
- I was on fire after that.
- You were getting the hang of it.

126
00:04:40,407 --> 00:04:41,707
It was really fun.

127
00:04:43,207 --> 00:04:44,377
He played the villain.

128
00:04:44,537 --> 00:04:45,677
We're in...

129
00:04:46,007 --> 00:04:47,406
We're in Dongjak-gu...

130
00:04:47,407 --> 00:04:49,346
- near Boramae Park, right?
- Boramae Park.

131
00:04:49,347 --> 00:04:50,376
- We passed Sangdo-dong.
- Right.

132
00:04:50,377 --> 00:04:51,737
Who has ties to this neighborhood?

133
00:04:52,077 --> 00:04:54,116
- Hae In lived here for a long time.
- It's Hae In.

134
00:04:54,117 --> 00:04:55,316
I briefly lived here.

135
00:04:55,317 --> 00:04:56,987
I live in Gyeonggi Province now.

136
00:04:57,317 --> 00:04:58,487
You moved?

137
00:04:58,887 --> 00:05:00,026
- I recently moved.
- Recently?

138
00:05:00,027 --> 00:05:01,033
- You recently moved?
- Yes.

139
00:05:01,057 --> 00:05:02,186
So...

140
00:05:02,187 --> 00:05:04,626
when we were filming the drama, we lived close to each other.

141
00:05:04,627 --> 00:05:05,627
- Really?
- Yes.

142
00:05:05,628 --> 00:05:07,567
- So this is your neighborhood?
- Yes.

143
00:05:07,797 --> 00:05:09,996
I've been living here for over 30 years.

144
00:05:09,997 --> 00:05:12,567
- I see. Really?
- It's been about 30 years.

145
00:05:12,667 --> 00:05:14,337
I did my military service around here.

146
00:05:14,437 --> 00:05:15,906
- Where?
- I was in the Air Force.

147
00:05:15,907 --> 00:05:17,137
He's mentioning that again.

148
00:05:17,737 --> 00:05:19,906
- What?
- He always brings up...

149
00:05:19,907 --> 00:05:21,627
his military service and Sejong University.

150
00:05:21,677 --> 00:05:23,216
- We're near Boramae Park.
- Come on.

151
00:05:23,217 --> 00:05:24,276
There's an Air Force base.

152
00:05:24,277 --> 00:05:26,016
- I was in the Air Force. So...
- I mean, I know that.

153
00:05:26,017 --> 00:05:27,723
Can't I mention that I was in the Air Force?

154
00:05:27,747 --> 00:05:29,787
His nickname is Jong.

155
00:05:30,257 --> 00:05:32,217
But I didn't bring up the university today.

156
00:05:32,257 --> 00:05:33,886
Seriously. The university...

157
00:05:33,887 --> 00:05:35,626
We shouldn't go to Gwangjin-gu.

158
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:36,997
They should give you an award.

159
00:05:37,427 --> 00:05:40,297
No one has put Sejong University on the map quite like Yeon Seok...

160
00:05:40,467 --> 00:05:42,266
besides Sejong the Great.

161
00:05:42,267 --> 00:05:44,367
- You know what's strange?
- I'm serious.

162
00:05:44,497 --> 00:05:45,796
I got invited...

163
00:05:45,797 --> 00:05:47,167
- for a Hangul Day event.
- Right?

164
00:05:47,467 --> 00:05:48,537
- See?
- I...

165
00:05:49,137 --> 00:05:51,677
Sejong University ought to do something nice for him.

166
00:05:53,847 --> 00:05:56,477
Anyway, you've been living around Boramae Park...

167
00:05:56,517 --> 00:05:58,116
- for 30 years.
- I've been here for a long time.

168
00:05:58,117 --> 00:05:59,663
You must've gone to a local high school then.

169
00:05:59,687 --> 00:06:01,186
Yes. I went to elementary, middle, and high schools...

170
00:06:01,187 --> 00:06:02,246
in this neighborhood.

171
00:06:02,247 --> 00:06:04,287
This is your hometown then.

172
00:06:04,317 --> 00:06:07,026
I grew up in Daebang-dong.

173
00:06:07,027 --> 00:06:08,156
- Gosh.
- Daebang-dong.

174
00:06:08,157 --> 00:06:10,697
- Daebang-dong...
- My base was in Daebang-dong.

175
00:06:11,897 --> 00:06:13,226
Across Military Manpower Administration.

176
00:06:13,227 --> 00:06:15,096
- Well, yes.
- I'm serious.

177
00:06:15,097 --> 00:06:16,336
- There's an Air Force base.
- Yes.

178
00:06:16,337 --> 00:06:18,967
But you don't live here anymore, right?

179
00:06:19,167 --> 00:06:21,006
- I still have ties here.
- Okay.

180
00:06:21,007 --> 00:06:22,936
My parents still live here.

181
00:06:22,937 --> 00:06:24,006
- I see. They live here.
- So you go back and forth.

182
00:06:24,007 --> 00:06:25,336
- Yes. I go back and forth.
- Your parents...

183
00:06:25,337 --> 00:06:27,947
I used to go to Boramae Park before my career took off.

184
00:06:27,977 --> 00:06:29,106
There's a boxed meal takeout place...

185
00:06:29,107 --> 00:06:30,246
in the basement of a department store.

186
00:06:30,247 --> 00:06:32,416
- I know the one.
- I bought a boxed meal...

187
00:06:32,417 --> 00:06:35,097
- and ate it at the park by myself.
- Did you practice at the park?

188
00:06:35,147 --> 00:06:36,217
I remember doing that.

189
00:06:36,387 --> 00:06:39,457
When I sometimes come here and want to go to a good restaurant,

190
00:06:39,927 --> 00:06:42,056
I remember Hae In and think about asking him for recommendations.

191
00:06:42,057 --> 00:06:43,796
- I hold myself back and never ask.
- Why not?

192
00:06:43,797 --> 00:06:44,996
- Why not? You should ask.
- You can ask.

193
00:06:44,997 --> 00:06:45,997
I mean, he's busy.

194
00:06:45,998 --> 00:06:47,296
I hearted a lot of places...

195
00:06:47,297 --> 00:06:49,103
- on Google Maps.
- Right. I saw a lot of hearts.

196
00:06:49,127 --> 00:06:50,996
- I see. The ones you saved?
- Yes. I saved a lot of places.

197
00:06:50,997 --> 00:06:52,836
- A tteokbokki stall and so on.
- Then...

198
00:06:52,837 --> 00:06:55,136
do you like going to famous restaurants?

199
00:06:55,137 --> 00:06:56,336
I like going to restaurants.

200
00:06:56,337 --> 00:06:58,006
- Hae In likes doing that.
- I see.

201
00:06:58,007 --> 00:06:59,546
- Yeon Seok and Hae In...
- Let's go to a good one today.

202
00:06:59,547 --> 00:07:00,576
Right.

203
00:07:00,577 --> 00:07:01,783
We don't have to worry about food today.

204
00:07:01,807 --> 00:07:04,647
What if you have to wait in line for over 30 minutes?

205
00:07:04,917 --> 00:07:06,187
Would you wait?

206
00:07:06,547 --> 00:07:09,416
- It's Friday today.
- Oh, right.

207
00:07:09,417 --> 00:07:11,763
When you see a line, do you give up instead of waiting in line?

208
00:07:11,787 --> 00:07:13,257
I... Right.

209
00:07:14,257 --> 00:07:15,257
(Satisfied)

210
00:07:15,257 --> 00:07:16,257
You don't wait in line?

211
00:07:16,258 --> 00:07:17,858
- No.
- You have a list, but don't wait?

212
00:07:17,957 --> 00:07:19,767
I have other places saved too.

213
00:07:19,997 --> 00:07:22,427
He goes to another restaurant he has saved.

214
00:07:22,667 --> 00:07:23,836
(That's the way to go.)

215
00:07:23,837 --> 00:07:26,166
I don't get stressed out...

216
00:07:26,167 --> 00:07:27,367
when a plan changes.

217
00:07:28,467 --> 00:07:30,106
- Your MBTI type ends with P.
- Yes.

218
00:07:30,107 --> 00:07:31,136
- What about you?
- Really?

219
00:07:31,137 --> 00:07:33,177
- Mine ends with P too.
- I see.

220
00:07:33,207 --> 00:07:35,106
Let's say I go to a famous restaurant...

221
00:07:35,107 --> 00:07:36,107
and there's a long line.

222
00:07:36,108 --> 00:07:37,116
- Do you...
- I eat at a convenience store...

223
00:07:37,117 --> 00:07:38,146
if there's one nearby.

224
00:07:38,147 --> 00:07:39,987
- I do that too.
- Really? I see.

225
00:07:40,187 --> 00:07:41,617
- I'm not like that.
- Okay.

226
00:07:41,947 --> 00:07:43,463
What about you, Sung Tae? What's your type?

227
00:07:43,487 --> 00:07:44,487
My type is F.

228
00:07:44,557 --> 00:07:45,587
No.

229
00:07:45,957 --> 00:07:47,127
Does it end with J or P?

230
00:07:47,757 --> 00:07:49,086
- Which one?
- It's J.

231
00:07:49,087 --> 00:07:50,396
- You're so clueless.
- I'm sorry.

232
00:07:50,397 --> 00:07:51,997
- "My type is F."
- It's INFJ.

233
00:07:52,657 --> 00:07:55,097
Why don't you say your type is X?

234
00:07:55,297 --> 00:07:56,697
Did you get an F in school or what?

235
00:07:57,367 --> 00:07:59,783
- You know what J stands for, right?
- Yes. They plan things.

236
00:07:59,807 --> 00:08:00,807
(Hold on.)

237
00:08:00,808 --> 00:08:02,066
Type P also plans things.

238
00:08:02,067 --> 00:08:03,837
I didn't call you guys out.

239
00:08:05,877 --> 00:08:07,006
We just don't like to plan things.

240
00:08:07,007 --> 00:08:08,007
- Right.
- Yes.

241
00:08:08,008 --> 00:08:10,417
- Anyway, we must get going today.
- Let's go.

242
00:08:10,877 --> 00:08:13,146
All right. Let's go and meet...

243
00:08:13,147 --> 00:08:14,747
the Whenever Friend from Dongjak-gu.

244
00:08:15,587 --> 00:08:16,716
Her name is Yoon Na Ra.

245
00:08:16,717 --> 00:08:17,816
- Na Ra.
- Yes.

246
00:08:17,817 --> 00:08:20,687
"I'm Dongjak-gu Fire Fist and want to give a boost..."

247
00:08:20,757 --> 00:08:22,056
"to our champion..."

248
00:08:22,057 --> 00:08:24,057
"who is set to embark on a new journey."

249
00:08:24,197 --> 00:08:25,427
They must be boxers.

250
00:08:25,697 --> 00:08:26,797
- Fire Fist.
- Right?

251
00:08:27,227 --> 00:08:29,196
"I'd like to invite the hosts..."

252
00:08:29,197 --> 00:08:32,096
"of Whenever Possible to our first sanctuary,"

253
00:08:32,097 --> 00:08:34,177
"steeped in sweat and memories for the final round."

254
00:08:34,567 --> 00:08:36,236
- Is it a gym?
- "Champion."

255
00:08:36,237 --> 00:08:38,336
"Final round." "Fire Fist."

256
00:08:38,337 --> 00:08:40,206
- Then it has to be a boxing gym.
- Do we have to box?

257
00:08:40,207 --> 00:08:41,623
- A boxing gym?
- It must be a boxing gym.

258
00:08:41,647 --> 00:08:42,706
Do you box, Sung Tae?

259
00:08:42,707 --> 00:08:44,547
- In our drama, - Do you box, Hae In?

260
00:08:44,717 --> 00:08:46,846
- I play a former boxer.
- I...

261
00:08:46,847 --> 00:08:48,886
But my character quit boxing...

262
00:08:48,887 --> 00:08:51,057
- and joined the gang.
- I see.

263
00:08:51,187 --> 00:08:52,386
He also plays a former boxer.

264
00:08:52,387 --> 00:08:54,556
- I also play a former boxer.
- He plays a former boxer.

265
00:08:54,557 --> 00:08:56,296
- Both of you play former boxers?
- So both of our characters...

266
00:08:56,297 --> 00:08:59,457
have something to do with boxing in the drama.

267
00:08:59,827 --> 00:09:02,627
I once played a boxer a long time ago too.

268
00:09:02,797 --> 00:09:04,013
- Really?
- It was a high school student.

269
00:09:04,037 --> 00:09:05,867
- Have you done any boxing before?
- Me?

270
00:09:06,367 --> 00:09:08,236
There was a segment called "Tomorrow's Champion."

271
00:09:08,237 --> 00:09:09,937
- Shim Hyung Rae was in it.
- Wait.

272
00:09:10,977 --> 00:09:12,477
- What?
- I loved that segment.

273
00:09:13,147 --> 00:09:14,507
- You liked that segment?
- Yes.

274
00:09:14,847 --> 00:09:16,477
You know the sound he made? That.

275
00:09:17,317 --> 00:09:19,476
It was called "Tomorrow's Champion." Shim Hyung Rae was in it.

276
00:09:19,477 --> 00:09:22,216
- How do I know that?
- It was a popular segment.

277
00:09:22,217 --> 00:09:23,856
- Hae In doesn't know it.
- I know it very well.

278
00:09:23,857 --> 00:09:25,557
- Of course, Sung Tae knows.
- I know too.

279
00:09:25,717 --> 00:09:27,586
(Responding right away)

280
00:09:27,587 --> 00:09:28,756
- His nickname was The Hisser.
- Right.

281
00:09:28,757 --> 00:09:30,757
Anyway, let's go. Where's the place?

282
00:09:31,427 --> 00:09:33,496
- We must be there by 12:30pm.
- We can get going now.

283
00:09:33,497 --> 00:09:34,796
Let me check the distance.

284
00:09:34,797 --> 00:09:37,667
- A boxing game?
- It takes 15 minutes on foot.

285
00:09:37,867 --> 00:09:38,867
Fifteen minutes?

286
00:09:38,868 --> 00:09:40,006
- Fifteen minutes on foot.
- Okay.

287
00:09:40,007 --> 00:09:41,487
- Let's walk there.
- Okay. Shall we?

288
00:09:43,007 --> 00:09:44,007
My gosh.

289
00:09:44,377 --> 00:09:46,107
- Goodness.
- The air feels incredibly hot.

290
00:09:49,917 --> 00:09:50,947
You know what?

291
00:09:51,377 --> 00:09:53,347
Every year, summer's getting hotter.

292
00:09:53,387 --> 00:09:54,587
- Right.
- Right?

293
00:09:54,817 --> 00:09:56,587
Back in the day, the highest temperature...

294
00:09:57,587 --> 00:10:00,026
- would be around 34°C.
- Exactly.

295
00:10:00,027 --> 00:10:01,356
- But now...
- It hit 40°C this year.

296
00:10:01,357 --> 00:10:02,486
- Daegu...
- It's over 40°C in the south.

297
00:10:02,487 --> 00:10:03,756
- It's 40°C in Daegu.
- Right.

298
00:10:03,757 --> 00:10:04,997
Gosh, this is a huge problem.

299
00:10:07,097 --> 00:10:08,537
- Hey, we can't.
- Stay on the left.

300
00:10:09,167 --> 00:10:10,167
Jae Seok, hold on.

301
00:10:10,168 --> 00:10:11,566
- Yeon Seok.
- Hold on.

302
00:10:11,567 --> 00:10:13,866
We must go with a different option. This is...

303
00:10:13,867 --> 00:10:15,107
We're feeling the heat and all.

304
00:10:15,307 --> 00:10:18,007
But we're the only ones walking on the street.

305
00:10:19,947 --> 00:10:21,476
- No one's out.
- Hold on.

306
00:10:21,477 --> 00:10:23,547
- Today...
- The heatwave alert was issued.

307
00:10:23,817 --> 00:10:25,116
Jae Seok, do you want to get on a bus...

308
00:10:25,117 --> 00:10:26,446
even if it's just for one stop?

309
00:10:26,447 --> 00:10:28,346
- Let's do it.
- A bus stop is across the street.

310
00:10:28,347 --> 00:10:29,347
- We should ride the bus.
- Great.

311
00:10:29,348 --> 00:10:31,508
- Let's ride it just for one stop.
- That sounds good.

312
00:10:31,917 --> 00:10:33,256
(Looking up the bus route)

313
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:35,026
My gosh. It's scorching hot today.

314
00:10:35,027 --> 00:10:36,426
(Glancing)

315
00:10:36,427 --> 00:10:37,457
You know what?

316
00:10:37,727 --> 00:10:38,926
Only you have a fan.

317
00:10:38,927 --> 00:10:39,967
Oh, this?

318
00:10:40,097 --> 00:10:42,466
My fan from Chiang Mai sent this to me. Thank you.

319
00:10:42,467 --> 00:10:44,296
- Really? Did you know?
- Hello, Chiang Mai.

320
00:10:44,297 --> 00:10:46,336
There's a handheld fan that blows cold air.

321
00:10:46,337 --> 00:10:49,036
- Right.
- It's right here.

322
00:10:49,037 --> 00:10:50,513
- It cools the air.
- It blows cold air.

323
00:10:50,537 --> 00:10:53,477
This fan doesn't suit your character in the drama.

324
00:10:54,077 --> 00:10:55,077
But I always...

325
00:10:55,078 --> 00:10:57,616
(He shows off his scary looks in the drama.)

326
00:10:57,617 --> 00:11:00,117
(But in real life, he just hates the heat.)

327
00:11:00,487 --> 00:11:02,216
- Is that the bus stop?
- Hold on.

328
00:11:02,217 --> 00:11:03,217
(They arrive at the bus stop before they melt.)

329
00:11:03,218 --> 00:11:05,138
- Is this the bus stop, Yeon Shik?
- Yes, it is.

330
00:11:07,027 --> 00:11:08,057
What's the bus number?

331
00:11:08,727 --> 00:11:11,056
I think that's the one. Bus 5516.

332
00:11:11,057 --> 00:11:12,596
- Is it coming?
- It's here.

333
00:11:12,597 --> 00:11:13,726
- Perfect timing.
- It's here.

334
00:11:13,727 --> 00:11:15,496
- Two stops?
- Yes, two stops.

335
00:11:15,497 --> 00:11:16,813
- Gosh, it's summer.
- Can you tag me in?

336
00:11:16,837 --> 00:11:18,696
- Hello.
- Hello.

337
00:11:18,697 --> 00:11:19,866
- Hello.
- Hello.

338
00:11:19,867 --> 00:11:20,967
- Hi.
- Yes.

339
00:11:21,437 --> 00:11:22,437
(Fully air-conditioned)

340
00:11:22,438 --> 00:11:24,158
- This is nice.
- Two stops. Gosh, my back.

341
00:11:24,777 --> 00:11:26,036
(Oh, we can finally breathe now.)

342
00:11:26,037 --> 00:11:28,346
- This is so nice.
- My gosh.

343
00:11:28,347 --> 00:11:29,407
Gosh, it's nice.

344
00:11:29,977 --> 00:11:32,617
It's only 15 minutes away on foot, but there's no way we can walk.

345
00:11:32,947 --> 00:11:36,087
Luckily, the bus turns right over there.

346
00:11:36,217 --> 00:11:38,516
- That's good.
- We'll get off at Seongdae Market.

347
00:11:38,517 --> 00:11:40,117
We just need to walk three more minutes.

348
00:11:40,287 --> 00:11:41,887
Your quick decision-making was great.

349
00:11:41,957 --> 00:11:43,056
- Seriously.
- Right?

350
00:11:43,057 --> 00:11:44,433
- That's good.
- Your quick thinking was great.

351
00:11:44,457 --> 00:11:47,567
We visit a lot of places every week when we film the show.

352
00:11:47,867 --> 00:11:49,427
I knew that it was just way too hot.

353
00:11:49,937 --> 00:11:52,367
- You felt it right away.
- I sensed that it was too hot.

354
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:54,667
(His fingers suddenly move fast.)

355
00:11:54,668 --> 00:11:56,108
It's tough for the staff and us too.

356
00:11:56,237 --> 00:11:57,477
- They could pass out.
- Right.

357
00:11:59,877 --> 00:12:00,877
Wait.

358
00:12:02,577 --> 00:12:03,617
What is it?

359
00:12:04,677 --> 00:12:05,817
What's wrong, Yeon Shik?

360
00:12:06,717 --> 00:12:08,277
- Is it the opposite direction?
- What?

361
00:12:08,317 --> 00:12:09,863
- Is it the opposite direction?
- What?

362
00:12:09,887 --> 00:12:11,787
- No, wait. Seongdae Market?
- What?

363
00:12:13,187 --> 00:12:14,627
No. This is the right direction.

364
00:12:14,787 --> 00:12:16,856
- No, this is the right way.
- It's the right direction.

365
00:12:16,857 --> 00:12:18,156
- It is?
- It is.

366
00:12:18,157 --> 00:12:20,267
- This is going to Seongdae Market?
- Yes. It is...

367
00:12:21,067 --> 00:12:23,166
- Hae In...
- Hold on.

368
00:12:23,167 --> 00:12:24,196
I have a bad feeling about this.

369
00:12:24,197 --> 00:12:25,236
- No.
- It's the right direction. Right?

370
00:12:25,237 --> 00:12:26,467
I know Seongdae Market.

371
00:12:26,607 --> 00:12:28,836
- Is this the right direction?
- If it's the opposite direction...

372
00:12:28,837 --> 00:12:30,113
We're heading to Seongdae Market.

373
00:12:30,137 --> 00:12:31,476
- Yeon Seok...
- Wait.

374
00:12:31,477 --> 00:12:32,906
- This is the right direction.
- Right?

375
00:12:32,907 --> 00:12:33,907
- Yes.
- The bus has to turn right here.

376
00:12:33,907 --> 00:12:34,907
- It will.
- Right.

377
00:12:34,908 --> 00:12:36,206
- It just did.
- It has to turn right.

378
00:12:36,207 --> 00:12:37,216
The bus has to.

379
00:12:37,217 --> 00:12:39,323
- They turn left on the other side.
- Let's press it.

380
00:12:39,347 --> 00:12:40,816
- Is it the opposite direction?
- Seongdae Market.

381
00:12:40,817 --> 00:12:42,046
- This is the right direction.
- Okay.

382
00:12:42,047 --> 00:12:43,787
- I see.
- We're getting off at this stop.

383
00:12:44,117 --> 00:12:45,316
- We're getting off here?
- Yes.

384
00:12:45,317 --> 00:12:49,386
- I'm starting to feel dizzy now.
- You got scared for nothing.

385
00:12:49,387 --> 00:12:50,856
- You gave me a good scare.
- Yes.

386
00:12:50,857 --> 00:12:52,296
- Yeon Shik.
- I feel dizzy.

387
00:12:52,297 --> 00:12:53,703
(Navi Yoo malfunctions due to the heatwave.)

388
00:12:53,727 --> 00:12:55,047
I got a bad feeling for a second.

389
00:12:55,367 --> 00:12:56,397
I'm suddenly sweating.

390
00:12:58,767 --> 00:12:59,836
(This Stop, Seongdae Market)

391
00:12:59,837 --> 00:13:01,167
- We're getting off here.
- Here.

392
00:13:03,507 --> 00:13:05,477
(Staring)

393
00:13:05,637 --> 00:13:06,957
"Boxing Club." Is that the place?

394
00:13:08,007 --> 00:13:09,383
It's that way. It should be around there.

395
00:13:09,407 --> 00:13:11,476
- I think that's the place.
- We can be there in three minutes.

396
00:13:11,477 --> 00:13:12,946
- You have a sharp eye.
- I caught it.

397
00:13:12,947 --> 00:13:14,587
(A boxing gym caught Jae Seok's eye.)

398
00:13:15,087 --> 00:13:16,146
(I'm Dongjak-gu Fire Fist...)

399
00:13:16,147 --> 00:13:17,987
(and want to give a boost to our champion...)

400
00:13:18,187 --> 00:13:20,526
(Will the first Whenever Friend be at the boxing gym as expected?)

401
00:13:20,527 --> 00:13:22,926
(They get off the bus.)

402
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,326
I think it's the boxing gym we passed by.

403
00:13:24,327 --> 00:13:25,626
- That's the only boxing gym.
- There.

404
00:13:25,627 --> 00:13:27,327
- The one on the second floor?
- Yes.

405
00:13:28,027 --> 00:13:29,267
I think this is the building.

406
00:13:29,567 --> 00:13:30,766
- Isn't it this building?
- It's right there.

407
00:13:30,767 --> 00:13:32,666
- "Boxing Club."
- Yes. It's on the third floor.

408
00:13:32,667 --> 00:13:33,836
- Right?
- Yes.

409
00:13:33,837 --> 00:13:35,157
- Jeon Jin Man.
- That's the one.

410
00:13:35,937 --> 00:13:37,806
(Dongjak-gu Fire Fists train here.)

411
00:13:37,807 --> 00:13:39,537
- This is the place.
- It's here.

412
00:13:41,677 --> 00:13:42,807
Hello.

413
00:13:44,977 --> 00:13:46,346
- Ms. Yoon Na Ra? Thank you.
- Hello.

414
00:13:46,347 --> 00:13:47,917
My gosh. You're the director.

415
00:13:49,017 --> 00:13:50,316
- Hello.
- Hello.

416
00:13:50,317 --> 00:13:51,516
- Hello.
- Hello.

417
00:13:51,517 --> 00:13:52,656
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

418
00:13:52,657 --> 00:13:54,886
Na Ra from the boxing gym wrote to us.

419
00:13:54,887 --> 00:13:55,926
Hello.

420
00:13:55,927 --> 00:13:59,596
- Are you Director Jeon Jin Man?
- Yes.

421
00:13:59,597 --> 00:14:02,326
You are the former champion.

422
00:14:02,327 --> 00:14:03,337
That's right.

423
00:14:03,967 --> 00:14:05,966
Judging by your name,

424
00:14:05,967 --> 00:14:08,006
I bet you were an infighter.

425
00:14:08,007 --> 00:14:09,206
- It sounds like "Charge forward."
- Your name...

426
00:14:09,207 --> 00:14:10,276
(Infighters tend to play aggressively.)

427
00:14:10,277 --> 00:14:12,077
- There's no backing away.
- No backing away.

428
00:14:12,177 --> 00:14:14,176
You don't look like an outboxer.

429
00:14:14,177 --> 00:14:16,277
(He only charges forward.)

430
00:14:16,617 --> 00:14:20,487
(Director Jeon Jin Man)

431
00:14:20,847 --> 00:14:22,716
(There's no backing away for Jeon Jin Man.)

432
00:14:22,717 --> 00:14:25,516
(WBO's last Asian Flyweight Champion)

433
00:14:25,517 --> 00:14:27,487
(A championship belt)

434
00:14:28,457 --> 00:14:29,826
(With his reputation as a champion on the line...)

435
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:32,426
How long have you been running the boxing gym?

436
00:14:32,427 --> 00:14:35,596
- I've been running it for 13 years.
- For about 13 years.

437
00:14:35,597 --> 00:14:37,896
Do you have a lot of members here?

438
00:14:37,897 --> 00:14:40,236
- Most of them are longtime members.
- I see.

439
00:14:40,237 --> 00:14:41,936
How long have you been training here, Na Ra?

440
00:14:41,937 --> 00:14:43,776
I've been a member here for six years.

441
00:14:43,777 --> 00:14:44,836
- That's a long time.
- And...

442
00:14:44,837 --> 00:14:47,176
- I was on maternity leave.
- Okay.

443
00:14:47,177 --> 00:14:48,476
So I've been training only for three years.

444
00:14:48,477 --> 00:14:49,746
- Three years?
- Yes.

445
00:14:49,747 --> 00:14:52,246
- Did you guys meet here?
- Yes.

446
00:14:52,247 --> 00:14:53,247
- Right.
- I see.

447
00:14:53,248 --> 00:14:57,116
Na Ra, what made you want to write to our show?

448
00:14:57,117 --> 00:15:00,186
He's going to relocate the boxing gym.

449
00:15:00,187 --> 00:15:03,396
He looked so stressed during the relocation process.

450
00:15:03,397 --> 00:15:05,026
It's been really tough.

451
00:15:05,027 --> 00:15:08,026
He said he lost 4kg.

452
00:15:08,027 --> 00:15:10,636
- He's going to move his gym.
- He seemed exhausted.

453
00:15:10,637 --> 00:15:11,796
I wanted to boost his energy.

454
00:15:11,797 --> 00:15:13,366
So you're relocating your gym?

455
00:15:13,367 --> 00:15:14,936
Yes. It's going to be in the new building...

456
00:15:14,937 --> 00:15:16,506
across the street.

457
00:15:16,507 --> 00:15:17,906
If it's in a new building,

458
00:15:17,907 --> 00:15:19,583
- aren't you expanding?
- Yes, I'm expanding.

459
00:15:19,607 --> 00:15:21,276
- You're expanding?
- Yes.

460
00:15:21,277 --> 00:15:22,777
That's good news. Why...

461
00:15:22,977 --> 00:15:25,176
But we've gotten attached...

462
00:15:25,177 --> 00:15:27,517
- to this place.
- I see.

463
00:15:28,247 --> 00:15:29,287
What a bummer.

464
00:15:29,747 --> 00:15:32,216
I worry about the possibility I might end up with fewer members...

465
00:15:32,217 --> 00:15:33,626
at the new place.

466
00:15:33,627 --> 00:15:35,057
That's a genuine concern for you.

467
00:15:35,087 --> 00:15:36,556
You're improving the facility.

468
00:15:36,557 --> 00:15:39,326
But you're worried about the business side of the gym.

469
00:15:39,327 --> 00:15:42,627
My gosh. So the director is expanding his business.

470
00:15:43,737 --> 00:15:46,497
- They seem genuinely happy.
- Have you seen this before?

471
00:15:46,567 --> 00:15:48,213
Have you ever met a genuine member like her?

472
00:15:48,237 --> 00:15:50,407
- She wrote a letter to us.
- She did.

473
00:15:50,737 --> 00:15:52,877
As for our members,

474
00:15:53,377 --> 00:15:55,576
they don't take my coaching for granted...

475
00:15:55,577 --> 00:15:57,376
even though they paid for my service.

476
00:15:57,377 --> 00:15:59,976
They're always grateful for my coaching...

477
00:15:59,977 --> 00:16:01,247
and try to take care of me.

478
00:16:01,687 --> 00:16:03,557
So we bonded more deeply.

479
00:16:04,457 --> 00:16:07,226
Where do you guys live then?

480
00:16:07,227 --> 00:16:08,786
- Do you live around here?
- Yes.

481
00:16:08,787 --> 00:16:11,056
When I was a newlywed,

482
00:16:11,057 --> 00:16:13,966
the director lived in a house behind mine.

483
00:16:13,967 --> 00:16:15,866
- Behind yours?
- So when I lived there,

484
00:16:15,867 --> 00:16:17,566
I opened the window to clean the windowsill.

485
00:16:17,567 --> 00:16:19,366
Then I saw him pass by.

486
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:20,907
I called him. "Director!"

487
00:16:21,267 --> 00:16:22,906
Then I moved.

488
00:16:22,907 --> 00:16:25,006
And Yeon Jung told me that she's his next-door neighbor now.

489
00:16:25,007 --> 00:16:27,406
We really do live next door to each other.

490
00:16:27,407 --> 00:16:30,176
The director drives a motorcycle.

491
00:16:30,177 --> 00:16:32,176
When I see the motorcycle parked at the house,

492
00:16:32,177 --> 00:16:34,287
I know that he's still home.

493
00:16:35,047 --> 00:16:37,386
There was a time I glanced over at his house...

494
00:16:37,387 --> 00:16:39,016
and came inside.

495
00:16:39,017 --> 00:16:40,017
(She can check his whereabouts through the window.)

496
